0003: fold a bindless UBO into const ranges only when the index is constant too.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Taken from the ArmadOS image recipe for
stack compatibility, not authored here; origin ROCKNIX (SM8550,
`patches/PATCHES.md`). Upstream: not in Mesa, never sent - not shown to be an
upstream bug from this bench.
**Found:** inherited; not reproduced here.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. The change makes the compiler less eager, never wrong-ward: a UBO
read through a dynamic bindless index keeps its real index.

## Summary

`ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c` folds UBO accesses into push-constant ranges. Stock
accepts a bindless access whose *resource* is constant even when the *index* is
dynamic; this change requires `nir_src_is_const(instr->src[1])` as well, so a
dynamic index is not attributed to one block.

## Evidence

One site, `get_ubo_info()` in `ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c`: one added condition.
No run here isolates the miscompile it prevents.

## Tests

Nothing here checks this hunk - it only matters for a bindless UBO indexed by a
uniform, which neither the 94-row matrix nor RE4 is known to compile. What would:
such a shader compiled both ways, compared in `IR3_SHADER_DEBUG` dumps.
NOT TESTED on this bench.

## The change in this repo

One hunk, one condition; it must not grow into a bindless rework. Revert:
`git apply -R` with the file name explicit.

## Related

`patches/PATCHES.md`.

